{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ועיני לאה רכות", :translit "v'einei leah rakhot", :gloss "and the eyes of Leah were tender"} {:he "ועיני ישראל כבדו מזוקן", :translit "v'einei yisrael kavdu mizoken", :gloss "and the eyes of Israel were heavy from old age"} {:he "ועיני רשעים תכלינה", :translit "v'einei resha'im techalnah", :gloss "and the eyes of the wicked will fail"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["ועיני לאה רכות" "ועיני ישראל כבדו מזוקן" "ועיני רשעים תכלינה"]}], :frame {:text "Leah's eyes were tender from weeping because people were saying, \"Laban has two daughters and the elder is for the elder\" — meaning Leah would marry Esau, and she wept and prayed until her eyelashes fell out (Bava Batra 123a). Jacob's eyes grew dim in old age from the distress of seeing that wicked descendants such as Jeroboam son of Nebat and Ahab son of Omri would come from him, as Rabba bar bar Channa said in the name of Rabbi Yochanan (Shabbat 152b) regarding the verse \"and the eyes of the wicked shall fail\" (Job 11:20). Ba'al HaTurim links all three verses: Leah's eyes and Jacob's eyes suffered on account of the wicked — Leah feared marrying Esau, and Jacob grieved over Jeroboam and Ahab.", :sources ["Bava Batra 123a" "Shabbat 152b" "Job 11:20"]}} {:quotes [{:he "רכות", :translit "rakhot", :gloss "tender"} {:he "ועיני לאה רכות", :translit "v'einei leah rakhot", :gloss "and the eyes of Leah were tender"} {:he "אם ידבר אליך רכות", :translit "im yedaber eleikha rakhot", :gloss "if he speaks tenderly to you"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ועיני לאה רכות" "אם ידבר אליך רכות"]}], :frame {:text "The phrase \"if he speaks tenderly to you\" appears in Proverbs 7:21, where the strange woman persuades a youth with smooth speech — yet her intentions are harmful. The verse at Genesis 29:31 states \"and the LORD saw that Leah was hated,\" confirming that despite her tender eyes, Jacob did not love Leah.", :sources ["Proverbs 7:21" "Genesis 29:31"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["ועיני לאה רכות" "ועיני ישראל כבדו מזוקן" "ועיני רשעים תכלינה"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ועיני לאה רכות", :refs ["Genesis 29:17"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ועיני ישראל כבדו מזוקן", :refs ["Genesis 48:10"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "ועיני רשעים תכלינה", :refs ["Job 11:20"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ועיני לאה רכות" "אם ידבר אליך רכות"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ועיני לאה רכות", :refs ["Genesis 29:17"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "אם ידבר אליך רכות", :refs ["Job 40:27"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:09:14.158646406Z", :model "glm-5.2"}